REM tajziya.pni: take one package from roadmap/packages.json to a proof.
REM © 1993–2026 Abhishek Choudhary. All rights reserved. AyeAI.
REM A cycler is a sequence of prompts and the outputs they produce. Edit it; it is not code.

CYCLER TAJZIYA
  TITLE   "One package, one proof"
  SCRIPT  "تجزیہ"
  OUTPUT  RESEARCH
  UNIT    "package"
  PURPOSE "Take one roadmap package for a classical-language node from open to proved."

  CONTRACT
    REFUSE    "rule text written from memory"
    REFUSE    "a reading chosen silently where the rules admit several"
    REFUSE    "a layer that answers before it is built"
    INVARIANT "a node is named by its registry id, never by a language name alone"
    EVIDENCE  "the acceptance command's output, pasted verbatim"
    EVIDENCE  "bash ops/verify.sh, pasted verbatim"
  END CONTRACT

  STAGE CONCEPT
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT JSON
    INTO   work
    ASK
      I am taking one package from roadmap/packages.json in the tajziya repository.
      Reply with only this JSON:
      {"package":"P-...","nodes":["registry node ids"],"true_when_done":"one sentence"}
      A node is a language at a stage, in declared scripts, holding a declared corpus, so
      name nodes by their registry id and never by a language name alone.
      What I have so far:
      {seed}
    END ASK
    VALIDATE HAS(work, "package")
    ON FAIL CLARIFY
  END STAGE

  STAGE SOURCE
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   VERIFY
    EXPECT JSON
    FROM   work
    INTO   work.sources
    ASK
      For every rule, table or word list this package brings in, give the source URL, the
      retrieval date, the SHA-256 of the bytes retrieved, and the terms under which they may be
      redistributed. Rule text from memory is not a source, however standard it looks.
      Material whose terms forbid reposting stays out of the tree; only its pin goes in.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE BOUNDS
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   MEASURE
    EXPECT JSON
    FROM   work
    INTO   work.bounds
    ASK
      List the conformance conditions in descriptor.json that this package touches, with each
      criterion copied verbatim. A condition that reads not established stays so unless it is
      measured here, and the measurement names its command.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE IMPLEMENT
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   work
    INTO   work.change
    ASK
      Write only inside the paths the package owns. A layer left unfinished still raises
      NotBuilt naming its package. Return every reading the rules admit and choose none.
      Where another package's paths are needed, stop and name that package instead.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE RUN
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   EXECUTE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   work
    INTO   work.run
    ASK
      Run the package's acceptance command exactly as written, then bash ops/verify.sh, and
      paste both outputs verbatim, failures included. A command that was not run is reported
      as not run.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE BREAK
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   FALSIFY
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   work
    INTO   work.falsify
    ASK
      Give one input on which this work would be wrong, and say whether it was run. Name any
      assumption carried over from another language or another stage without a source.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE ATTACH
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   INTEGRATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   work
    INTO   work.attach
    ASK
      Name which of the four attachment points in INTEGRATION.md this work crossed. If it
      needed a fifth, say so plainly: that is a contract question, not settled here.
    END ASK
    GATE   HUMAN "PROOF accepted"
  END STAGE
END CYCLER
